---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { RATE_CATEGORIES, BASIS, DATA_DATE_LABEL, fmtUsd, fmtRange } from '../lib/site';
import { alpha, categoryStats } from '../lib/rates';

const listings = (await getCollection('listings')).sort(alpha);
const withRates = listings.filter((l) => l.data.rates.length > 0);
const stats = RATE_CATEGORIES.map((c) => ({ ...c, ...categoryStats(listings, c.id) }));

// Light jet bar chart: rows that apply to light jets only, sorted by low end.
const lightRows = categoryStats(listings, 'light').rows.slice().sort((a, b) => a.rate.low - b.rate.low);
const SCALE = 10000;
const pct = (n: number) => Math.min(100, (n / SCALE) * 100);

const cell = (l: any, cat: string) => {
  const rows = l.data.rates.filter((r: any) => r.category === cat);
  if (!rows.length) return '';
  return rows.map((r: any) => fmtRange(r.low, r.high) + (r.shared ? ' *' : '') + (rows.length > 1 ? ` (${r.label})` : '')).join('; ');
};
const shown = RATE_CATEGORIES;

const med = categoryStats(listings, 'midsize');
const heavy = categoryStats(listings, 'heavy');
const lightS = categoryStats(listings, 'light');
const range = (s: { min: number | null; max: number | null }) => `${fmtUsd(s.min!)} to ${fmtUsd(s.max!)}`;
const faq = [
  {
    q: 'How much does a private jet charter cost per hour?',
    a: `Providers publish very different figures. Across the providers we read, light jets are published at ${range(lightS)} an hour (${lightS.providers} providers), midsize jets at ${range(med)} (${med.providers}) and heavy jets at ${range(heavy)} (${heavy.providers}). These are marketing figures read from each provider's own pages on ${DATA_DATE_LABEL}. Some are base rates and some are all-in, and none is a quote.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Why do published hourly rates differ so much?',
    a: 'Providers publish different things under the same label. A base rate covers the aircraft and crew, with fees and taxes added. An all-in figure divides a total trip price by flight time, so it includes positioning, daily minimums, fees and tax. JetLevel says its all-in figures run higher than advertised base rates for that reason. Several pages do not say which kind of figure they show.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the hourly rate the price I will pay?',
    a: 'No. Billable time can include positioning and a daily minimum, and fees and taxes come on top. One broker publishes a sample trip where a $3,400 hourly rate over 5 flight hours came to $20,317.50 after fuel, crew, landing fees and a 7.5% federal excise tax. The FAA lists a $5.30 per-passenger segment tax for 2026. Ask for an itemized written total.',
  },
];
const jsonLd = [
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebPage', name: 'Private jet charter cost per hour: what providers publish', description: 'Hourly rates published by private jet charter providers, with the basis labeled.' },
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Private Jet Charter Cost Per Hour: Published Rates Compared" description={`Hourly rates ${withRates.length} charter providers publish by aircraft type, labeled base or all-in and linked to each page. Light jets run ${range(lightS)} an hour.`} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="wrap prose wide">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Published rates</p>
    <h1>Private jet charter cost per hour: what providers publish</h1>
    <p class="lead">What each provider's own pages say a flight hour costs, by aircraft type. Read on {DATA_DATE_LABEL}. These are marketing figures, not quotes.</p>

    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Read this before the numbers</h2>
      <p>The tables below are <strong>not like for like</strong>. Providers publish three different things under the same label:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>{BASIS.base.label}.</strong> The price of the aircraft and crew by the hour. The provider says fees, taxes or positioning come on top.</li>
        <li><strong>{BASIS['all-in'].label} and {BASIS.planning.label.toLowerCase()}.</strong> A total trip price spread over flight time, or a range meant for budgeting. These run higher because they include positioning, minimums and fees.</li>
        <li><strong>{BASIS.unstated.label}.</strong> The page does not say. We do not guess.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>One provider, JetLevel, says this directly: many published hourly rates are an aircraft's base rate, and its own all-in figures are higher for that reason. For the other high-range pages the cause is not stated, so we do not claim it.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Light jets, as published</h2>
    <p>Each bar is the provider's published range on a scale of $0 to {fmtUsd(SCALE)} an hour. The color says what the page says the figure includes.</p>
    <div class="legend">
      <span class="tag base">Base rate</span>
      <span class="tag all-in">All-in or planning range</span>
      <span class="tag unstated">Basis not stated, or a starting price</span>
    </div>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="stack">
        <caption>Light jet hourly rates, {new Set(lightRows.map((r) => r.id)).size} providers</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Published</th><th scope="col">Basis</th><th scope="col">Range<div class="axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>$0</span><span>$2k</span><span>$4k</span><span>$6k</span><span>$8k</span><span>$10k</span></div></th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {lightRows.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><a href={`/listings/${r.id}/`}>{r.name}</a>{lightRows.filter((x) => x.id === r.id).length > 1 && <span class="small"><br />{r.rate.label}</span>}</th>
              <td data-label="Published" class="num">{fmtRange(r.rate.low, r.rate.high)}</td>
              <td data-label="Basis"><span class={`tag ${r.basis}`}>{BASIS[r.basis].label}</span></td>
              <td data-label="Range">
                <div class="bar" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class={`fill ${r.basis}`} style={`left:${pct(r.rate.low)}%;width:${r.rate.high === null ? 1.5 : Math.max(1.5, pct(r.rate.high) - pct(r.rate.low))}%`}></span>
                </div>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small">"From" prices have no upper end and show as a marker. Paramount Business Jets publishes separate light and super light rows; both are shown as light here. Mercury Jets gives one range for turboprop and light jets together, so it is left out of this chart.</p>

    <h2>Every category</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="dense">
        <caption>Published hourly rates by provider and aircraft type (USD)</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Basis</th>{shown.map((c) => <th scope="col">{c.label}</th>)}</tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {withRates.map((l) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><a href={`/listings/${l.id}/`}>{l.data.name}</a></th>
              <td><span class={`tag ${l.data.rateBasis}`}>{BASIS[l.data.rateBasis].label}</span></td>
              {shown.map((c) => <td class="num">{cell(l, c.id) || '-'}</td>)}
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small">* One range given for two categories. "-" means no figure for that category on the pages we read. Providers with no published price are on the <a href="/providers/">providers page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Spread by category</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="stack">
        <caption>Lowest and highest published figure in each category (single-category rows only; mixes base, all-in and planning figures)</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Aircraft type</th><th scope="col">Providers</th><th scope="col">Lowest low</th><th scope="col">Highest high</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {stats.filter((s) => s.providers > 0).map((s) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{s.label}</th>
              <td data-label="Providers" class="num">{s.providers}</td>
              <td data-label="Lowest low" class="num">{s.min ? fmtUsd(s.min) : '-'}</td>
              <td data-label="Highest high" class="num">{s.max ? fmtUsd(s.max) : 'none stated'}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <dl class="faq">
      {faq.map((f) => (<><dt>{f.q}</dt><dd>{f.a}</dd></>))}
    </dl>

    <h2>How to use this</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask each provider whether its number is a base rate or an all-in trip price, and ask for the total in writing.</li>
      <li>Do not multiply an hourly rate by flight time. Billable time can include positioning and a daily minimum. See <a href="/fees/">fees</a>.</li>
      <li>If a provider lists no price, that is a finding, not a mark against it. Many sell by quote. They are on the <a href="/providers/">providers page</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
